{"Title":"An Act to regulate school enrollment ","BillNumber":"H484","DocketNumber":"HD1336","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:11:03.09"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:11:03.09"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H484/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 484) of Colleen M. Garry for legislation to establish an opt-out admissions lottery process for charter schools.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSubsection (n) of Section 89 of chapter 71 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2012\r\n\tOfficial Edition, is hereby amended by striking out the first sentence and inserting in place thereof\r\n\tthe following two sentences:-\r\n\tEnrollment in a commonwealth charter school shall use an opt-out admissions lottery process that automatically includes the names of all eligible students, without any required application process for the school.  A commonwealth charter school’s tuition payment shall be adjusted to account for any students who cannot attend said school because necessary services are not available.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}